  "notes": [
    "First sweep is published. The confirmation sweep is drift evidence only; the faster sweep is never selected.",
    "Natural-suite decode throughput pools measured samples as sum(decode_tokens)/sum(decode_seconds). decode_tokens is 127 per sample (generated tokens minus the first observed cumulative count), so first-token latency, prefill, and MTP prompt priming are excluded.",
    "Whole-call throughput pools sum(generated_tokens)/sum(whole_call_seconds) and includes prefill and first-token latency, so it is not comparable to the decode rate.",
    "Per-length values are medians of per-sample rates, not ratios of pooled sums.",
    "Candidate acceptance is sum(accepted_counts)/sum(candidate_counts) over measured MTP samples; the candidate budget is one per cycle.",
    "AR/MTP id equality is a cross-route diagnostic, not a same-schedule repeatability check.",
    "Drift flags are reported for review and do not block publication; the summary never chooses between sweeps.",
    "MTP route counters do not reconcile with the decode window: cycles plus accepted candidates sum to 11390 for 90 measured natural-suite samples, while the 127-per-sample post-first-token count implies 11430. Treat cycle and acceptance counts as route-reported and do not derive token throughput from them."
  ]
